      "statement": "Cilium 1.17.0 adds services protocol differentiation, enabled by default and controllable with the cilium-agent flag --bpf-lb-proto-diff; after the upgrade, existing Services without a protocol set are preserved as such and must be deleted and recreated for their protocol to be taken into account by the agent."
    },
    "corrected": {
      "applicability": {
        "exposure": {
          "op": "all",
          "of": [
            {
              "op": "edge-from-version",
              "state": "in-range",
              "range": "<1.17.0"
            },
            {
              "op": "not",
              "of": [
                {
                  "op": "cli-flag",
                  "name": "--bpf-lb-proto-diff",
                  "component": "cilium-agent",
                  "state": "equals",
                  "values": [
                    "\"false\""
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "overlap": {
          "op": "all",
          "of": [
            {
              "op": "edge-from-version",
              "state": "in-range",
              "range": "<1.17.0"
            },
            {
              "op": "cli-flag",
              "name": "--bpf-lb-proto-diff",
              "component": "cilium-agent",
              "state": "equals",
              "values": [
                "\"false\""
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "statement": "Exposed: environments upgrading to 1.17.0 from a version below 1.17.0 with services protocol differentiation on (the default). Their existing services keep no protocol until deleted and recreated. Environments that set --bpf-lb-proto-diff=false are shielded."
    },
